# Whiteboard Diagram Skill

This project contains a universal skill for generating hand-drawn whiteboard diagrams.

When asked to create any whiteboard, diagram, hand-drawn board, sketch, or visual architecture:

1. Read SKILL.md for comprehensive instructions on generating hand-drawn diagrams
2. Default output: Mermaid with `look: handDrawn` (works everywhere)
3. Alternative outputs: SVG (standalone), Excalidraw JSON (editable), HTML (interactive)
4. Always apply: sketchy borders, pastel color fills, icons/emojis, numbered sections, connecting arrows
5. Use the 6 curated pastel palettes from SKILL.md
6. Follow the layout patterns: Grid, Flow, Layers, Kanban, Mind Map, Comparison
7. Check references/ directory for extended color palettes, layout patterns, and code examples
